package ai

import "strings"

// One on-demand reference owns signatures and facts, never task strategy.
func computerScriptHelp(topic string, browser bool) (string, bool) {
	core := `UI/browser operations are async and awaited sequentially; the script has no DOM, timers, Node, filesystem or network globals. ui.snapshot({root_ref?,limit?:1..1000,emit?:boolean,full?:boolean,on_invalidated?:'throw'|'return'}) -> {document_id,url?,title?,nodes,total,truncated} | {status:'invalidated',reason:'document_changed',observation_stage,invalidation?,needs_observation:true} without content when on_invalidated='return'. Defaults: limit=200, emit=true, full=false, on_invalidated='throw'. Automatic output is bounded tree text; guest values retain nodes. read_options is a method inventory, not per-node support. ui.observe(options) returns {observation,...metadata} or the same invalidated value. ui.screenshot() emits an image and returns a frame-bound handle. log(...values) emits JSON-compatible values; ordinary return values are not emitted.
ui.ref(ref:string) and ui.getByRole(role:string,{name?:string,exact?:boolean,root_ref?:string}) -> locator. Names use case-insensitive contains matching unless exact=true; RegExp is unsupported. Unique operations reject zero/multiple matches. locator.node() -> node; locator.read() -> {node}; locator.snapshot(options) -> subtree snapshot or the same invalidated value. node() is a bounded single-node projection: parent_ref is optional and absent relationships are not evidence of source absence.
locator.click(options?), locator.fill(text), locator.press(key), locator.scroll(delta_y,delta_x=0), locator.waitFor({state?,timeout_ms?}) -> result; locator.requireState(options) -> void or CONDITION_TIMEOUT. ui.type(text), ui.key(key), ui.click(x,y), ui.doubleClick(x,y), ui.drag(x1,y1,x2,y2,duration_ms=0), ui.scroll(delta_y,delta_x=0), ui.scrollAt(x,y,delta_y,delta_x=0). Input results report delivery, not application success.
ui.help(topic='core') emits and returns a string. ui.capabilities() returns target conditions. ui.budget() -> {remaining_ms,remaining_operations,remaining_log_bytes,log_limit_bytes}. const/let are call-local; globalThis is healthy thread/turn/target scoped. context_reset clears script state, not the thread's saved target. Example: await ui.snapshot();`
	if topic == "" || topic == "core" {
		if browser {
			return core + `
Browser: browser.navigate(url,options?), browser.back(options?), browser.reload(options?) -> lifecycle receipt. locator.query({limit?,cursor?}) -> {items,total,truncated,next_cursor?}; locator.count() -> number; locator.rows({limit?,cursor?}) -> {rows,total,truncated,next_cursor?} for one table/grid; locator.text() -> {text,truncated,...identity} for an HTML element. Snapshot/query/rows totals cover loaded AX content only. locator.attribute(name) -> string|null; locator.source(options?) reads original fields in chunks (details: source); locator.geometry(options?) returns geometry. click/hover preparation defaults: scroll_into_view=false, stability_timeout_ms=0. Example: const value=await ui.ref('observed-ref').text(); log(value); Details: read, source, interaction, visual, navigation, downloads, runtime, legacy.`, true
		}
		return core + `
Native coordinates are window-local points. DOM and collection methods are browser-only. Details: read, source, interaction, visual, runtime, legacy.`, true
	}
	switch topic {
	case "read":
		common := `Snapshots retain canonical role, platform_role, ref, name, states, child_refs and optional value/description. Relations link returned nodes; parent_ref is optional. Fields are bounded to 2,000 Unicode code points with independent *_truncated flags. source_truncated identifies collection loss; output_truncated identifies presentation loss; truncated covers either. full=true changes output shape, not collection limits.
Tree text has JSON-quoted refs, roles and names followed by key=JSON facts. Indentation denotes parentage; parent_ref overrides it. Frame identity inherits only within a full emitted view, with frame_absent/frame_document_absent marking absence. Model text is bounded to 32 KiB including JSON encoding; title/URL prefixes have explicit loss flags. No implicit diff or content ranking.
Readonly methods accept {on_invalidated:'throw'|'return'}. return produces {status:'invalidated',reason:'document_changed',observation_stage,invalidation?,needs_observation:true} without content only for typed no-effect document changes; permission, cancellation and unknown failures still stop. Source/continuation identity does not establish application readiness.`
		if !browser {
			return common + "\nNative snapshots contain application-provided AX content. Native locator.source() exposes enumerated AX fields and source relations; DOM/collection methods are unavailable.", true
		}
		return common + `
locator.query({limit?:1..200,cursor?}) -> {items:[{ref,role,platform_role,name,name_truncated?}],total,truncated,next_cursor?,scope:'loaded_accessibility_tree'}; default limit=50. locator.count(options?) -> total. Ordering is source AX child order within frames; ref queries match that node, not descendants.
locator.rows({limit?:1..200,cursor?}) -> {rows:[{ref,cells:[{ref?,role,text}]}],total,truncated,next_cursor?,scope:'loaded_accessibility_tree',source:'browser_ax',property:'name'}. It requires one table/grid. Header roles and cells_truncated/text_truncated are retained. Totals count loaded rows; cursors expire when source changes.
locator.text(options?) -> {text,truncated,scope:'element',source:'browser_dom',property:'innerText',...identity}. Maximum 12,000 code points; no additional visibility filtering. Only HTML elements are supported; document/text/SVG nodes return TARGET_CAPABILITY_UNAVAILABLE, without parent substitution.
locator.attribute(name,options?) -> string|null; locator.getAttribute(name,options?) -> {attribute,value,redacted?}. Exact nonempty DOM attribute name <=2,000 characters; value over 2,000 code points fails without a partial scalar. Empty and null differ. Relative URLs/query/fragment remain source values; URL credentials are redacted. linkSummary is retired and rejects with precise_attribute_read.`, true
	case "source":
		return `locator.source({source?:'ax'|'dom',field?:string,limit?:1..12000,cursor?:string,parameter?,on_invalidated?}). Default source=ax. With no field it enumerates source field names; otherwise returns {source,document_id,ref,encoding:'text'|'json',value,offset,total,unit:'unicode_code_points',truncated,next_cursor?}. JSON chunks are prefixes, not independently valid JSON. Source changes invalidate cursors.
child_refs and native AX element arrays return {items,offset,total,unit:'items',truncated,next_cursor?}, up to 200 refs per page. These source relations can extend beyond compact snapshot relations; source refs may be read-only or DOM-less and do not grant input authority. Native supports AX and parameterized:<name> with parameter:{location,length}. Browser supports AX and DOM; DOM fields include attribute:<name>, textContent, innerText, value, hidden, offscreen and child_refs. No source value is inferred from a missing projected field. Unavailable/no_value differs from empty. All reads retain permission/privacy checks and bounded ref retention. Example: log(await ui.ref('observed-ref').source()); enumerates field names before an explicit field read.`, true
	case "interaction":
		return `locator.click({button?:'left'|'right'|'middle',modifiers?:['Alt'|'Control'|'Meta'|'Shift'],click_count?:1..3,duration_ms?:0..5000,point?,scroll_into_view?,stability_timeout_ms?}); locator.hover({point?,scroll_into_view?,stability_timeout_ms?}). Browser-only preparation defaults false/0; requested stability_timeout_ms is integer 0..5000. point is {x,y} in session CSS pixels. The fixed first content-quad center (or supplied point) is both hit-tested and dispatched; no alternate-point search. Geometry/identity/hit checks remain mandatory. locator.geometry({point?,on_invalidated?}) returns quads, viewport, coordinate_space, source identity and optional hit_target. Rejections expose actionability.failed_checks, geometry samples, preparation and elapsed_ms.
fill(text) replaces content; ui.type(text) inserts at current focus. key/press accepts a character or named key with Alt/Control/Meta/Shift, e.g. Enter, ArrowDown, Meta+=; physical Equal is unsupported. press requires focusability. Explicit clipboard shortcuts through key/input are rejected.
locator.selection() returns UTF-16 ranges; selectText(text,{prefix?,suffix?,selection_type?:'text'|'cursor_before'|'cursor_after'}), selectRange(start,end,{direction?:'forward'|'backward'|'none'}), selectAll(), replaceSelection(text), copy(), cut(), paste({text?,html?}). Ranges cannot split surrogate pairs; native permits omitted/none direction. ui.clipboard('types'|'read'|'write',{items?}) uses maps of MIME/pasteboard type to base64 bytes, max 64 KiB. System clipboard access requires Full access and browser/OS permission. Supplied paste retains supplied clipboard content; consumption cannot be confirmed.
setValue(value) invokes supported native AX values or browser input values with synthetic events; performAction(name) invokes a discovered native AX action. Browser setFiles([{name,mime_type,base64}]) supplies <=16 files/256 KiB encoded bytes to the exact file input with synthetic events, without filesystem reads.
ui.input(events) sends <=100 explicit keyDown/keyUp, mouseMoved/mousePressed/mouseReleased and wait transitions. Key events: {type,key,modifiers?,repeat?}; pointer: {type,x,y,button?,buttons?,modifiers?,click_count?}; wait: {type:'wait',duration_ms:0..5000}, total wait <=30000. Cancellation releases task-owned held input, never replays transitions. Native foreground operations retain foreground consent; background-directed input has no foreground fallback.`, true
	case "visual":
		return `ui.screenshot(options?) emits an image and returns metadata plus an immutable handle. handle.hover(x,y), click(x,y,clickOptions?), doubleClick(x,y), drag(x1,y1,x2,y2,duration_ms=0), scroll(x,y,delta_y,delta_x=0) use the optimized displayed image pixels; captured frame/document identity cannot be retargeted by editing metadata. Handles expire on namespace reset/turn/target changes. Changed document/viewport rejects stale input.
Screenshot image:{locator,width,height,coordinate_space:'original_image_pixels'} identifies the admitted original for image_read({locator,crop:{x,y,width,height}}). Crop uses original pixels and grants no input authority. No PNG bytes/filesystem path is returned by ui.screenshot.
Direct browser ui coordinates use CSS viewport pixels; native coordinates are window-local points matching normalized screenshot pixels. Native AX bounds share those coordinates. Drag duration_ms is integer 0..5000; 0 adds no delay; delivery overhead may extend the straight held path. Scroll deltas are pixels, positive down/right. Browser scroll_progress describes the exact sampled element/viewport with before/after/offset_changed, measurement:'immediate_after_dispatch',scroll_effect:'unknown'; null/unchanged offsets do not establish page-level outcome. No scrolling-container inference or input repetition.`, true
	case "navigation":
		if !browser {
			return "Navigation is browser-only.", true
		}
		return `browser.navigate(url,options?), browser.back(options?), browser.reload(options?). options:{wait_until?:'commit'|'domcontentloaded'|'load',timeout_ms?:0..30000}; defaults load/20000. Returns {command_acknowledged,navigation_stage,wait:{state:'reached'|'timeout',wait_until,timeout_ms,elapsed_ms},same_document?}; downloads return navigation_stage:'download',download_started:true without a document wait. Lifecycle timeout is data; network errors stop. A receipt contains no page content and does not establish application readiness. Destination permission and target control remain mandatory. No navigation replay or automatic page read.`, true
	case "downloads":
		if !browser {
			return "Downloads are browser-only.", true
		}
		return `browser.downloadCursor() -> {cursor,downloads,wait(options?)}; handle.wait({timeout_ms?}) binds the captured cursor. browser.waitForDownload({after:string,timeout_ms?}) or ({id:string,timeout_ms?}) returns download identity/state. Exactly one of after/id is required. Multiple new downloads return AMBIGUOUS_DOWNLOAD with IDs. browser.saveDownload(id) -> {id,filename,path,size_bytes,state:'saved'}, max 256 MiB. browser.readDownload(id,{offset?:0,limit?:1..65536}) -> {id,filename,offset,bytes,base64,size_bytes?,truncated,next_offset?}; default limit=16384. Methods read only selected-source downloads, never arbitrary filesystem paths.`, true
	case "runtime":
		return `One invocation: <=50 operations, <=30 seconds, 64 MiB heap. SCRIPT_OPERATION_LIMIT stops before operation 51 with budget_exhausted='operations' and context_reset=true; completed effects remain and are not replayed. No DOM, timers, Node, filesystem, network or raw CDP. Operations are awaited sequentially; concurrent operations are rejected. snapshot/observe/locator.snapshot emit automatically unless emit=false; help/screenshots always emit; other reads return guest data.
Output budgets are independent: log(...values) JSON-encodes its argument array, with <=65,536 UTF-8 bytes per invocation. log(value) retains structured values; stringifying first emits a JSON string. Automatic observations have a separate 384 KiB encoded aggregate budget; compact snapshot tree text is <=32 KiB including metadata and JSON escaping, while structured semantic snapshots are <=256 KiB. emit=false suppresses automatic output without reducing guest nodes or their log cost. An oversized log is not emitted; SCRIPT_OUTPUT_LIMIT stops execution with context_reset=true, retaining earlier output, completed reads and output_limit facts. It does not mean a completed read failed. Private pauses remove content.
Result outline (optional fields marked ?): {status,truncated,data:{completed,completed_actions,operations,context_reset,truncated,logs?,observations?,completed_reads?,read_outcomes?,output_limit?,...}}. completed_actions lists completed operations; completed_reads retains read kinds/scopes. read_outcomes entries contain zero-based operation_index,action,status and observed identity; collection reads also retain total,returned_count,truncated. Snapshot/observe receipts additionally retain source_truncated,scope and explicit root_ref/limit, including emit=false reads.
The outer truncated and data.truncated describe delivery loss, not source completeness. read_outcomes[].truncated describes that source page; snapshot source_truncated describes source collection loss. In emitted compact observations, source_truncated describes collection loss, output_truncated describes presentation loss, and truncated is either. A delivered result can have outer truncated=false with source_truncated=true. Counts and flags do not establish application readiness. Explicit collection pagination and source-field continuation are documented in read/source.
Execution failures retire the namespace/dormant promises with context_reset=true; parse-only failures can retain a healthy namespace. Resetting script state does not clear the thread's saved target. globalThis lasts only in that healthy thread/turn/target; const/let are call-local. SCRIPT_NO_PROGRESS means unresolved script with no pending supported operation. Any failed host operation seals the invocation even if caught.
completed_actions records completed operations, not preparation/partial input. input_progress, preparation_executed, failed_operation_index/phase, stop_reason, budget_exhausted and effect_outcome_unknown are independent facts. Unknown effects never establish non-execution. Typed pre-dispatch failures report action_executed=false. The runtime performs no automatic replay/reselection.
locator.waitFor({state?:'visible'|'hidden'|'enabled',timeout_ms?:0..30000}) returns {state}; defaults visible/10000. Browser also supports {state:'text'|'value',equals:string}. Browser wait facts include requested_state,timeout_ms,elapsed_ms,samples; timeout is data. locator.requireState(options) uses the same condition and throws CONDITION_TIMEOUT on timeout. Explicit waits sample the original query under the requested deadline; no input is repeated or scope widened. Privacy, target identity, cancellation and resource limits remain enforced.`, true
	case "legacy":
		return computerLegacyScriptDocumentation, true
	default:
		return "", false
	}
}

func computerBrowserTarget(kind string) bool { return strings.HasPrefix(kind, "browser.") }
